# .mutation-allowlist - surviving (LIVED) mutants accepted as already known.
#
# SCOPE: this allowlist covers ONLY the packages inside the mutation gate scope
# (see MUTATE_EXCLUDE in the Makefile): internal/cli, internal/db, internal/model,
# internal/config and internal/tui. Mutations outside that scope are not run at
# all, so they can never appear here. cmd/ is still excluded: it is the entry point
# with no logic of its own.
#
# Format:  <MUTATOR> <file>:<line>
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY. 0 entries.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# It once held 40 entries and now holds none. The 40 were not deleted: they were
# killed. Each was one of these four shapes, and all four were fixed by
# changing the code, not the list:
#
# 1. "THE CLAMP IS AN IDENTITY AT THE EDGE".
#    `if len(x) > n { x = x[:n] }`. When len(x) == n the slice is the same, so
#    `>` and `>=` give the same result and no test separates them. It is now
#    `x[:min(len(x), n)]`, which has no edge to mutate. In detail.go, tag_modal.go,
#    fuzzy.go, kanban.go and layout.go.
#
# 2. "THE EDGE DOES NOT EXIST BECAUSE OF ARITHMETIC".
#    A float never falls exactly on epsilon, so `capacity <= epsilon` and
#    `remaining > epsilon` had no input that separated them. The gantt now does
#    its arithmetic in whole MINUTES, where `free == 0` is reached with any round
#    estimate. And where the problem was comparing against 0 --
#    `x <= 0` and `x < 1` are the SAME condition over integers, so its mutant
#    was unkillable -- it now compares against 1, which has a real edge.
#
# 3. "THE COMPARISON IS INSIDE A LOOP".
#    The `max(min(...))` inside a loop whose range only produced safe values.
#    By extracting the arithmetic into a pure function (stepGanttCursor), the
#    cursor becomes a parameter and a test can feed it negatives and values past
#    the list. Same with estimateNoNegativo and esImprimible.
#
# 4. "THE COMPARISON DID NOT PRODUCE A NUMBER, BUT A DECISION".
#    An `if` that can be removed because what the function below does already
#    covers it. The case was `if end-start <= visible { return }` in listWindowForHeight:
#    visibleRange with size >= total returns the whole page, so the guard was
#    redundant. And the two sort comparators in fuzzy.go, now a cmp.
#
# The file is kept, and cannot be deleted, because the mutation workflow uses it
# to calibrate: without it the job is skipped instead of reporting green while
# measuring nothing. Empty means ANY survivor is a failure, which is correct
# when there truly are none.
#
# Add an entry ONLY when the mutant is provably equivalent (no test can ever kill
# it, because the mutation does not change observable behaviour) or the gap is a
# conscious, accepted risk. Adding a real test gap here hides a real risk, and
# mutation testing exists precisely to surface those.
#
# Entries are keyed by LINE NUMBER, so inserting code above an entry shifts it
# and will surface a new red on purpose: re-verify the gap and update this file,
# do not regenerate it wholesale (that would silently re-hide real gaps).